Who Needs A Heart When A Heart Can Be Broken?

2
00:13:06,666 --> 00:13:12,666
What's Love Got to Do with It is a drama, music,
history film directed by Brian Gibson.

3
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Singer Tina Turner rises to stardom while mustering the
courage to break free from her abusive husband Ike.

4
00:26:13,333 --> 00:26:19,333
Anna Mae Bullock / Tina Turner, played by Angela Bassett.

5
00:32:46,666 --> 00:32:52,666
Ike Turner, played by Laurence Fishburne.

6
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:26,000
Jackie, played by Vanessa Bell Calloway.

7
00:45:53,333 --> 00:45:59,333
Zelma Bullock, played by Jenifer Lewis.

8
00:52:26,666 --> 00:52:32,666
Darlene, played by Khandi Alexander.

9
00:59:00,000 --> 00:59:06,000
Ike Turner Jr., played by Richard T. Jones.

10
01:05:33,333 --> 01:05:39,333
What's Love Got to Do with It is a 1993 American biographical film
based on the life of singer-songwriter Tina Turner.

11
01:12:06,666 --> 01:12:12,666
Directed by Brian Gibson and written by Kate Lanier from an uncredited story draft by the late Howard Ashman, based on Tina's 1986
autobiography I, Tina, it stars Angela Bassett as Tina and Laurence Fishburne as her abusive husband Ike Turner.

12
01:18:40,000 --> 01:18:46,000
What's Love Got to Do with It premiered in Los Angeles on June 6, 1993, and was
theatrically released by Touchstone Pictures on June 25, 1993.

13
01:25:13,333 --> 01:25:19,333
Although the Turners disapproved of its inaccuracies, the film was critically and
commercially successful, grossing $61 million on a $15 million budget.

14
01:31:46,666 --> 01:31:52,666
For their performances, Bassett and Fishburne received nominations at
the 66th Academy Awards for Best Actress and Best Actor.

15
01:38:20,000 --> 01:38:26,000
Bassett also won the Golden Globe Award for Best
Actress – Motion Picture Comedy or Musical.

16
01:44:53,333 --> 01:44:59,333
The film explores themes of 1970s, affectation, record
producer, biography, recording studio.

17
01:51:26,666 --> 01:51:32,666
The tone is uplifting and emotional.
